#question(title: [More True or False], shrink: true)[
  #set text(size: 13pt)

  Let $f$ and $g$ be differentiable functions
  with domain $display(RR)$.  \
  Assume that $display(f' (x) = g(x))$ for
  all $x$.  \
  Which of the following statements must be
  true?

  + $display(f(x) = integral_0^x g(t) d t)$.
  + If $display(f(0) = 0)$, then
    $display(f(x) = integral_0^x g(t) d t)$.
  + If $display(g(0) = 0)$, then
    $display(f(x) = integral_0^x g(t) d t)$.
  + There exists $C in RR$ such that
    $display(f(x) = C + integral_0^x g(t) d t)$.
  + There exists $C in RR$ such that
    $display(f(x) = C + integral_1^x g(t) d t)$.
]
